  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "For real numbers \\(a\\) and \\(b,\\) define \\(a\\,\\$\\,b=(a-b)^2.\\) What is \\((x-y)^2\\,\\$\\,(y-x)^2?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(x^2+y^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(2x^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(2y^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(4xy\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": "0"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2008-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\((y-x)^2=(x-y)^2,\\) the two inputs are identical.\n\nTherefore \\((x-y)^2\\,\\$\\,(y-x)^2\\) \\(=\\left((x-y)^2-(x-y)^2\\right)^2\\) \\(=0^2=0.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Compare \\((x-y)^2\\) and \\((y-x)^2\\)",
        "Once you know the two inputs agree, apply the definition of \\(a\\,\\$\\,b\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
